Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:32:16 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 35/48] avformat/mov: read the auxiliary type of items and
 tracks, depth included

The auxiliary type of a HEIF item (auxC, ISO/IEC 23008-12) and of an
auxiliary video track (auxi) names alpha or depth, for HEVC
(urn:mpeg:hevc:2015:auxid:N), AVC (urn:mpeg:avc:2015:auxid:N) and any
codec (urn:mpeg:mpegB:cicp:systems:auxiliary:alpha and :depth). Export it
as the stream's AV_PKT_DATA_AUXILIARY_ID, 1 for alpha and 2 for depth
(H.265 Table F.2).

The aux_subtype of an HEVC depth item carries SEI NAL units, each after
its 32-bit size, after the 32-bit size of them all, as libheif reads them
from cameras' images: export the depth representation information
message (H.265 G.14.2.4) as AV_PKT_DATA_DEPTH_REPRESENTATION_INFO.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
---
Refreshed for FFmpeg 9.1 (deb-multimedia 10:9.1-dmo1), 2026-11-26: FFmpeg 9.1 moved the item reference and display matrix code into mov_parse_heif_item_references(), and added its own auxC reader (gain map and alpha flags on HEIF items) with its own parse table entry. One reader stays: this patch's (bounded read, the AuxId of the exact type, the depth aux_subtype) with 9.1's two flags set by 9.1's own matching; 9.1's definition and this patch's second table entry for auxC are gone. The auxiliary type and depth representation side data follow the stream's disposition as before.

